msvc/
downloads/

# === Runtime Local Storage (NEVER commit raw or metadata files) ===
/storage/
# The eval corpus is deliberately split across this line. `/storage/eval/` holds the entity
# payloads and the annotation worksheets, which carry the customer's Japanese drawing text and
# are the same confidentiality class as the DXFs above. The reviewable half —
# `tests/fixtures/eval/manifest.json` plus the hand-authored label files — IS tracked: it is
# sha256 digests, pair ids, drawing numbers and category counts, no drawing content. Do not
# "fix" this by tracking the payloads. See infrastructure/eval/corpus.py.
services/storage/uploads/
# The `/storage/` rule above is anchored to the repo root, so it does NOT cover the
# backend's own storage tree — which is how services/backend/storage/secure/.api-token
# came to be committed. That token is generated at startup by
# core/security.py::initialize_local_api_token and regenerates if absent.
#
# Written as `/*` rather than as a bare directory on purpose: git never descends into an
# excluded *directory*, so `services/backend/storage/` would make every `!` rule below it
# unreachable no matter what order they appear in. Excluding the contents instead keeps the
# same effect while leaving one door openable.
services/backend/storage/*

# Stage 0h: the learned model moved out of the gitignored vault, because a model that cannot
# be committed, diffed or shipped is not trainable infrastructure — it blocked rung 3.
# The `.joblib` payload stays untracked (it is a build artifact); the `.meta.json` beside it
# is tracked, so every training run is diffable in git without carrying a binary.
!services/backend/storage/models/
services/backend/storage/models/*
!services/backend/storage/models/*.meta.json

